# Licensing

Copyright © 2026 EvolvLabs, LLC.

This repository uses **two licences**: one for code, one for the writing.

## Code — MIT

The MIT License ([`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](LICENSES/MIT.txt)) covers:

- `scripts/`, `tests/`, `.github/`, `schema/`, `site/`
- `pyproject.toml`, `manifest.json` and every `pack.meta.json`, `sources.json`
  and `regions/*.json` file (configuration and metadata, not prose)

## Writing — CC BY-NC 4.0

Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
([`LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt),
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/>) covers:

- everything under `packs/*/sources/` — quick cards (`cards.json`), library
  documents (`docs/*.md`) and map overlays
- `README.md` files

In plain words (the licence text is what counts):

- You may copy, share and adapt this writing **for non-commercial use**.
- You must credit **Holdfast / EvolvLabs, LLC**, link this licence, and **say
  what you changed**. For survival and first-aid text this matters: a changed
  card must never look like ours.
- You may not use it primarily for commercial advantage or money — for
  example in a paid app, an app with in-app purchases or ads, or a product for
  sale. Ask us if you want to.

EvolvLabs, LLC, as the owner, is not bound by these terms and uses this writing
in the Holdfast app, which is free and takes optional tips.

**Public-domain sources stay public domain.** Our cards and documents are
written from US government guidance (FEMA, CDC, USDA, NOAA, US Army). Those
sources remain free for anyone to use for any purpose; this licence covers only
our own wording, selection and arrangement.

## Contributions

By opening a pull request or otherwise submitting material to this repository,
you agree that:

1. it is your own work, or you have the right to submit it under these terms;
2. code you submit is licensed under MIT, and writing under CC BY-NC 4.0, like
   the rest of this repository; and
3. you also grant EvolvLabs, LLC a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
   royalty-free, irrevocable licence to use, copy, modify, distribute and
   sublicense your contribution for any purpose, including commercially, so it
   can ship in the Holdfast app.

## Third-party content (not covered by either licence)

The two licences above apply **only to material written in this repository**.
Everything downloaded or linked keeps its own licence, which the manifest
records per pack in `license` and `attribution`:

| Pack | Licence of the content itself |
| --- | --- |
| `core` | CC BY-NC 4.0 (our writing); underlying guidance public domain (FEMA, CDC, NOAA, Red Cross) |
| `medical` | Hesperian terms **unconfirmed — linked, not hosted**; WikiMed CC BY-SA 4.0 |
| `water-food` | public domain (CDC, EPA, USDA) |
| `manuals` | public domain (US Army, FEMA) |
| `maps-roads-*` | ODbL 1.0 — © OpenStreetMap contributors, credit must appear on the map |
| `maps-topo-*` | public domain (USGS 3DEP) |
| `maps-routing-*` | ODbL 1.0 — derived from the same OSM extract |
| `shelter-repair` | CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (iFixit) — **non-commercial**; recheck if anything is ever sold |
| `wikipedia-top50k` | CC BY-SA 4.0 — Wikipedia contributors |
| `offline-ai-model` | Apache-2.0 — Qwen3-1.7B (Alibaba Cloud) |
| `offline-ai-embedder` | Apache-2.0 — sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 |

Rules the spec sets, which no licence choice here changes:

- **Public-domain US government material** (Army, FEMA, CDC, EPA, USDA, NOAA,
  USGS) may be hosted and modified freely. Credit the source anyway.
- **Share-alike material** (Wikipedia, Stack Exchange, OpenStreetMap) may be
  redistributed with attribution; the credit shows on each pack's About screen
  and, for maps, on the map itself.
- **Non-commercial material** (iFixit) is fine for a free app and must be
  rechecked if anything is ever sold or bundled into a paid product.
- **Free but copyrighted material** (Hesperian) is linked, never hosted, until
  redistribution terms are confirmed in writing.
- Content changes go through the same pull-request review as code, and medical
  content is reviewed before release.
